---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "July 7, 2026";

const sections = [
  { id: "who-we-are", label: "Who We Are" },
  { id: "summary", label: "Summary" },
  { id: "data-we-collect", label: "Data We Collect" },
  { id: "permissions", label: "Permissions We Request" },
  { id: "third-parties", label: "Third-Party Services" },
  { id: "future-features", label: "Upcoming Paid Features" },
  { id: "retention", label: "Data Retention & Deletion" },
  { id: "children", label: "Children's Privacy" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes To This Policy" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact" },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Open Citadel"
  description="How Open Citadel handles your data: what stays on your device, what we never see, and what changes when you opt into paid cloud features."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24 px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-20 bg-obsidian">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex flex-col gap-16">
      <!-- Header -->
      <header class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <p
          class="font-body text-xs font-semibold text-gold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] m-0"
        >
          Legal
        </p>
        <h1
          class="font-display text-parchment m-0 leading-[1.1]"
          style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 400;"
        >
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="font-body text-sm text-parchment-dim m-0">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Table of contents -->
      <nav
        aria-label="Table of contents"
        class="bg-surface-low p-6 md:p-8"
        style="border: 1px solid rgba(208,197,175,0.08);"
      >
        <p
          class="font-body text-xs font-semibold text-gold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] m-0 mb-4"
        >
          On this page
        </p>
        <ul class="list-none m-0 p-0 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-2">
          {
            sections.map(({ id, label }) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`#${id}`}
                  class="font-body text-sm text-parchment-dim hover:text-gold transition-colors no-underline"
                >
                  {label}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <!-- Body -->
      <article
        class="font-body text-parchment-dim leading-relaxed flex flex-col gap-14"
      >
        <p class="m-0">
          Open Citadel is built on a simple premise: your notes, your
          reading, and your thinking are yours. This policy explains exactly
          what data the app touches, where it lives, and what — if anything —
          leaves your device.
        </p>

        <section id="who-we-are" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Who We Are
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Open Citadel is developed by <strong class="text-parchment"
              >Thamsanqa Ncube</strong
            >, registered as an individual developer on Google Play. There is
            no separate company entity at this time; this policy will be
            updated to reflect the responsible entity if that changes in the
            future.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="summary" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Summary
          </h2>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5 m-0">
            <li>
              Everything you create in Open Citadel — books, notes,
              highlights, timeline entries — is stored in a local database on
              your device. We do not operate a server that stores your
              content.
            </li>
            <li>
              The app does not require account creation or sign-in, and we do
              not collect your name, email, or other personal information.
            </li>
            <li>
              We do not sell data, show ads, or use third-party tracking or
              advertising SDKs.
            </li>
            <li>
              The app connects to the internet only to download AI models
              you choose to use (from Hugging Face) — never to transmit your
              notes or reading data.
            </li>
            <li>
              Paid features (milestone/goal/task tracking, and an optional
              cloud AI tier) are in development and not yet available. See <a
                href="#future-features"
                class="text-gold hover:opacity-80">Upcoming Paid Features</a
              > for how this policy will change when they ship.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="data-we-collect" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Data We Collect
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            As of this version of the app, Open Citadel does not collect,
            transmit, or store any of your personal data on servers we
            operate. All content you add — books, highlights, notes,
            timeline entries, and downloaded AI models — is stored in a local
            SQLite database on your device, inside the app's private storage.
            We have no access to this data, and it is never sent anywhere by
            the app.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            We do not use analytics, crash-reporting, or advertising SDKs
            inside the app itself.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="permissions" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Permissions We Request
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">The Android app requests the following:</p>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5 m-0">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-parchment">Storage</strong> — to let you import
              books/documents into your library and export or save images (e.g.
              highlight cards) to your device's gallery. Files you pick or export
              are only accessed with your explicit action.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-parchment">Internet</strong> — to download
              AI models you select (served from Hugging Face) and, for the future
              cloud AI tier described below, to send requests to that service.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="third-parties" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Third-Party Services
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            <strong class="text-parchment">Hugging Face</strong> — when you choose
            to download an on-device AI model (e.g. Gemma, Qwen, DeepSeek), the
            app downloads that model file directly from Hugging Face's public
            hosting. This is an anonymous file download; the app does not attach
            any personal or usage data to these requests.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            <strong class="text-parchment">Google Play Billing</strong> — when
            paid features launch, purchases will be processed entirely by Google
            Play. We will not see or store your payment details; Google's own
            <a
              href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-gold hover:opacity-80">privacy policy</a
            > governs that data.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0 text-sm" style="opacity: 0.8;">
            Note: this website (the page you're reading now) uses Vercel Web
            Analytics to count anonymous, aggregated page views. This is
            separate from the app and does not use cookies or collect
            personal data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="future-features" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Upcoming Paid Features
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Open Citadel currently ships as a free, fully on-device app with
            no accounts. We are building paid features — milestone, goal, and
            task tracking/review, plus an optional cloud AI tier — which are
            not yet available. Here is what to expect, and what will change
            in this policy before each ships:
          </p>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-parchment"
                >Milestone, goal, and task tracking</strong
              > will work the same way your other data does today: stored locally
              on your device. It does not by itself introduce any new data leaving
              your device.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-parchment">Cloud AI tier</strong> will be an
              optional, opt-in upgrade for running AI conversations in the cloud
              instead of on-device. When enabled, the content of your messages
              and the context needed to generate a response will be sent to <a
                href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-gold hover:opacity-80">OpenRouter</a
              >, a third-party AI model routing service we use to process
              those requests. OpenRouter's own privacy policy governs how they
              handle that data. This feature will be off by default, clearly
              labeled in the app, and will never be applied to content you
              haven't explicitly sent to it.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="m-0">
            Before either feature is released, we will update this policy
            with the full, specific details (including any additional
            processors involved and data retention practices) and note the
            change in the app's update notes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Data Retention & Deletion
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Because your content lives in a local database on your device,
            you are always in control of it. You can delete individual books,
            models, or notes from within the app, or remove all app data by
            uninstalling Open Citadel — this permanently deletes the local
            database, and we have no copy to retain.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="children" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Children's Privacy
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Open Citadel is not directed at children under 13, and we do not
            knowingly collect personal information from children.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Changes To This Policy
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            We may update this policy as the app evolves, particularly as
            paid features launch. The "Last updated" date at the top of this
            page will always reflect the most recent revision, and material
            changes will be called out in the app's release notes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <h2 class="font-display text-gold text-2xl font-medium m-0">
            Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Questions about this policy or your data can be sent to <a
              href="mailto:thamsanqa.dev@gmail.com"
              class="text-gold hover:opacity-80">thamsanqa.dev@gmail.com</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
